# Subscriber Churn & Wearable Biometric Attrition Analysis

**Author:** Shehram Khan  
**Domain:** Health & Fitness Operations / Subscription Retention Analytics  
**Tech Stack:** Python 3.10, Pandas, NumPy, Scikit-Learn, Matplotlib, Seaborn, Jupyter Notebook  

---

## Project Overview

Commercial fitness clubs and connected wellness applications routinely experience annual subscriber churn between 40% and 55%, with cancellations heavily concentrated in the first five months of membership. Because acquiring a new member costs 5x to 7x more than retaining an existing subscriber, relying on lagging administrative triggers—such as failed monthly billing or 30 days of turnstile inactivity—leaves operators too little time to intervene before exercise habits collapse.

This project builds an end-to-end machine learning classification and risk-stratification pipeline that pairs commercial club membership records with longitudinal wearable sensor telemetry. By engineering sports-science workload indices—specifically the **4-Week Workout Decay Ratio** and **Acute-to-Chronic Workload Ratio (ACWR)**—the model identifies early behavioral drift weeks before financial cancellation occurs.

